DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssaavvee--eennttrrooppyy command is used to save entropy data from _/_d_e_v_/_r_a_n_d_o_m to
     files in a specified output location.  The files saved are used at
     startup to provide additional entropy for _/_d_e_v_/_r_a_n_d_o_m.  The output file
     will be different in every invocation until the maximum number of differ‐
     ent files is reached.  (See _e_n_t_r_o_p_y___s_a_v_e___n_u_m for details).  By default
     this script is invoked via cron(8) every eleven minutes approximately.

     This command does nothing if executed inside a jail(8).

     Three variables in _/_e_t_c_/_r_c_._c_o_n_f regulate the behavior of the script:

     _e_n_t_r_o_p_y___d_i_r
